  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">World Organisation for Animal Health (WOAH): Core contribution</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australian Government is party to the International Agreement for the Creation at Paris of an International office for Dealing with Contagious Disease of Animals, and Annex (1925) Treaty. The World Organisation for Animal Health (WOAH) is the international standard setting body for animal health and welfare. WOAH also supports its members to improve their governance mechanisms and to strengthen the capacity of their Veterinary Services to increase compliance with WOAH international standards.</narrative>
  </description>
